# SEQ-BONE-KEYS: bone transform keys in the Level Sequencer, layered over the Animation track (UE FK Control Rig).
# Humanoid's bones are Hips..Head, Shoulder.L.. (Editor/Resources/Engine/Meshes/Skinned/Humanoid.skeleton); its idle clip is "Idle".
# A document value is a number: Bone.<actor>.<bone>.Blend is 0 Absolute, 1 Additive; Rotation is Euler degrees (pitch, yaw, roll).
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/SEQ_BoneKeys.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано run Document "Sequencer: New Level Sequence Sequences/SEQ_BoneKeys.dseq"
Дано run Document "Sequencer: Add Actor Hero"
Дано run Document "Sequencer: Add Actor Twin"
Дано run Document "Sequencer: Add Animation Hero Idle"
Дано run Document "Sequencer: Add Animation Twin Idle"
# [1_base] no bone tracks: both play idle, heads forward.
Когда set Transport.Time 1.0
Тогда-вид 1_base both humanoids stand in idle, heads facing the camera, arms down; identical poses
# [2_absolute] Hero head yaw 45 deg, absolute, weight 1.
Когда run Document "Sequencer: Add Bone Track Hero Head"
Когда set Bone.Hero.Head.Rotation 0,45,0
Когда run Document "Sequencer: Key Bone Hero Head"
Тогда-вид 2_absolute Hero's head is turned about 45 deg to its left, body still in idle; Twin's head faces the camera (same bone name, other actor untouched); the Sequencer shows a Head row under Hero with a key at 1.0 s
Тогда 2_absolute lua World.find('Hero'):boneLocalRotation('Head') yaw (y) = 45 +-0.5; World.find('Twin'):boneLocalRotation('Head') = idle value +-0.5; editor.log has no "names no entity"
# [3_weight] weight 0.5 blends with the idle pose, not with zero.
Когда set Bone.Hero.Head.Weight 0.5
Тогда-вид 3_weight Hero's head is turned about half as far as in 2_absolute (~22 deg), not drooped or collapsed
# [4_additive] additive 15 deg over idle: the idle breathing still moves the head.
Когда set Bone.Hero.Head.Weight 1.0
Когда set Bone.Hero.Head.Blend 1
Когда set Bone.Hero.Head.Rotation 0,15,0
Когда run Document "Sequencer: Key Bone Hero Head"
Тогда-вид 4_additive Hero's head turned slightly (~15 deg) to its left on top of idle; arms and torso as in 1_base
# [5_scrub] scrub away and back: same frame.
Когда set Transport.Time 0.0
Когда set Transport.Time 1.0
Тогда-вид 5_scrub identical to 4_additive (pixel diff only in idle-free regions = 0)
# [6_play] Play mode: runtime path, same pose as the scrub; step key 0 -> 45 at t=1.0 (Constant) checks lag and UpdateRate.
Когда set Bone.Hero.Head.Blend 0
Когда set Transport.Time 1.0
Когда set Bone.Hero.Head.Rotation 0,45,0
Когда run Document "Sequencer: Key Bone Hero Head"
Когда run Action Play
Когда advance 1.0
Тогда 6_play Hero head yaw (lua boneLocalRotation('Head').y) = 45 +-0.5 on the first frame at t>=1.0 (no frame of lag), also with Animation.UpdateRate 2
# [7_stop] leaving Play and closing the Sequencer removes the layer.
Когда run Action Stop
Когда run Document "Sequencer: Close"
Тогда-вид 7_stop both humanoids as in 1_base: Hero's head faces the camera again
# [8_undo] undo the bone track: no row, no turned head.
Когда run Open "Sequences/SEQ_BoneKeys.dseq"
Когда run Action Undo
Тогда-вид 8_undo Sequencer has no Head row under Hero; Hero in idle
# [9_refused] a bone the rig lacks is refused by name (no "Add Bone Track Hero tail_01" action exists: the menu lists the skeleton's bones).
Когда set Bone.Hero.tail_01.Rotation 0,10,0
Тогда 9_refused Output Log names "tail_01" and Hero's skeleton ("tail_01: the skeleton of Hero has no such bone"); no row added; 0 VUID in editor.log
